{"title":"2010 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Alternative_method:\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Alternative method:</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bf65a0e5e2500d1c001daa3e603356bf4bc931.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x^6-10x^5+29x^4-4x^3+ax^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"265\" height=\"18\" /> lies above the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/6/416ae37947d4f62622823098de22e5fcf4a0b875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=bx+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" /> except at three values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, where the graph and the line intersect. What is the largest of these values?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/ccefe446ac26b1d2ff26fd59aaaea8ce281b5a83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 7 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> values in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bf65a0e5e2500d1c001daa3e603356bf4bc931.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x^6-10x^5+29x^4-4x^3+ax^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"265\" height=\"18\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/6/416ae37947d4f62622823098de22e5fcf4a0b875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=bx+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" /> are the same as the zeros of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/d/2ddb02974f8059914806e9cb0f0bb7d1837ee4c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x^6-10x^5+29x^4-4x^3+ax^2-bx-c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"337\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> zeros and the function is never negative, all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> zeros must be double roots because the function's degree is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the roots of this function, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/a/83a85d9907b4104c6d4cf670f440645e3b206669.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3-ux^2+vx-w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"145\" height=\"16\" /> be the cubic polynomial with roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/6/1c69b49db1f012e936a64ac252b8641a8e392756.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}(x-p)(x-q)(x-r) &amp;= x^3-ux^2+vx-w\\\\ (x-p)^2(x-q)^2(x-r)^2 &amp;= x^6-10x^5+29x^4-4x^3+ax^2-bx-c = 0\\\\ \\sqrt{x^6-10x^5+29x^4-4x^3+ax^2-bx-c} &amp;= x^3-ux^2+vx-w = 0\\end{align*}\" width=\"678\" height=\"74\" />\n</p><p>In order to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/f/06fbb72fc8f7dbd7d2d5f414ad038678539b9032.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^6-10x^5+29x^4-4x^3+ax^2-bx-c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"319\" height=\"18\" /> we must first expand out the terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/2715ede67a7036c7bad854f06a15d394e6800c1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^3-ux^2+vx-w)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"166\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d16c66369fc2eddcf00659452090770548ed7b2f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x^3-ux^2+vx-w)^2\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/0/eb002a07ca7ea06f1283bf510ee1f32a40a4324f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= x^6-2ux^5+(u^2+2v)x^4-(2uv+2w)x^3+(2uw+v^2)x^2-2vwx+w^2\\]\" width=\"496\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>[Quick note: Since we don't know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, we really don't even need the last 3 terms of the expansion.]\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3baf78dfd19a18270e11d507b63997111ad9f8be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}&amp;2u = 10\\\\ u^2+2v &amp;= 29\\\\ 2uv+2w &amp;= 4\\\\ u &amp;= 5\\\\ v &amp;= 2\\\\ w &amp;= -8\\\\ &amp;\\sqrt{x^6-10x^5+29x^4-4x^3+ax^2-bx-c} = x^3-5x^2+2x+8\\end{align*}\" width=\"555\" height=\"171\" />\n</p><p>All that's left is to find the largest root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/c/c1c5b397f295def2d8eafb5cbc6b58950812f008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3-5x^2+2x+8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"139\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/2/cf2369021c156f71636a4ca0af65c44da9efac34.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}&amp;x^3-5x^2+2x+8 = (x-4)(x-2)(x+1)\\\\ &amp;\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 4}\\end{align*}\" width=\"330\" height=\"55\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> values in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bf65a0e5e2500d1c001daa3e603356bf4bc931.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x^6-10x^5+29x^4-4x^3+ax^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"265\" height=\"18\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/6/416ae37947d4f62622823098de22e5fcf4a0b875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=bx+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" /> are the same as the zeros of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/d/2ddb02974f8059914806e9cb0f0bb7d1837ee4c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x^6-10x^5+29x^4-4x^3+ax^2-bx-c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"337\" height=\"18\" />.\nWe also know that this graph has 3 places tangent to the x-axis, which means that each root has to have a multiplicity of 2.\nLet the function be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/f/cffe3af76227000fa8e9025cd121ec4848e17e3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-p)^2(x-q)^2(x-r)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p><p>Applying Vieta's formulas, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/5/00540d831a8294caf5c16d4587d3712b73319354.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2p+2q+2r = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"140\" height=\"16\" />  or  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/4/fd4e810881f140610dea3842e113f0eff01b66f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q+r = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />.\nApplying it again, we get, after simplification, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6b6d4937506b6df93d37c1e99648b9a9d9fcba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2+q^2+r^2+4pq+4pr+4qr = 29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"283\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Notice that squaring the first equation yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/a/58a771f3596dbb09786b8fa35c719206ce5406f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2+q^2+r^2+2pq+2qr+2pr= 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"283\" height=\"18\" />, which is similar to the second equation.\n</p><p>Subtracting this from the second equation, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/8/a3886a5bb4f3fcbe397937fb10978c491a04b6ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2pq+2pr+2qr = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"160\" height=\"17\" />. Now that we have the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/7/b5798edc20aa63959af65f2ee1d0aa7cca9864f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pq+pr+qr$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"14\" /> term, we can manpulate the equations to \nyield the sum of squares. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/8201cd54e07d678b96f2732610ecf70040119d4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(p^2+q^2+r^2+2pq+2qr+2pr)-2pq-2pr-2qr= 25*2-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"511\" height=\"19\" /> or  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/b/69beb6bc837f11ceabfa56589e252d6cf1ffc040.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2p^2+2q^2+2r^2+2pq+2qr+2pr = 46$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"309\" height=\"18\" />. We finally reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/f/85fcfad87039fb34a2e7af4d48d721564dec4521.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p+q)^2+(q+r)^2+(p+r)^2 = 46$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"271\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p><p>Since the answer choices are integers, we can guess and check squares to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/4/a942cbdbedfc89aa1615f99efbd5877ffc379d13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{(p+q)^2, (q+r)^2, (p+r)^2\\} = \\{1, 9, 36\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"316\" height=\"21\" /> in some order. We can check that this works by adding then and seeing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/5/00540d831a8294caf5c16d4587d3712b73319354.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2p+2q+2r = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"140\" height=\"16\" />. We just need to take the lowest value in the set, square root it, and subtract the resulting value from 5 to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/3502fb5e69be78d9b9580690026667f60fc47147.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>Note: One could also multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/8/a3886a5bb4f3fcbe397937fb10978c491a04b6ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2pq+2pr+2qr = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"160\" height=\"17\" /> by 2 and subtract from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6b6d4937506b6df93d37c1e99648b9a9d9fcba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2+q^2+r^2+4pq+4pr+4qr = 29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"283\" height=\"18\" /> to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b583f1ec8923af18f17715e3fbebc23e57450c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p^2+q^2+r^2=21\\]\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" /> The ordered triple {16,4,1} sums to 21, and the answer choices are all positive integers, therefore the answer is 4. \n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alternative_method:\">Alternative method:</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Alternative method:\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>After reaching <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/4/fd4e810881f140610dea3842e113f0eff01b66f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q+r = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/b/eeb5a8c2acb82e1c21caa4dd8c89e368cc4e59dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pq + qr + rp = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"131\" height=\"15\" />, we can algebraically derive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/7/63795f5ae81b5558afc51ffd1b2e8a7a30d38f30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pqr$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p><p>Applying Vieta's formulas on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/48524d3889ec8433cb03669176e738011df245b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> term yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/2/0a2c485ce2dff855b720b70857da36c6ea9a92bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2p^2q+2pq^2+2q^2r+2qr^2+2r^2p+2rp^2+8pqr = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"408\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/7/b87722212830b7e560aaa839f906cce9d343e176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p+q+r)(pq+qr+rp) = p^2q+pq^2+q^2r+qr^2+r^2p+rp^2+3pqr$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"541\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/8/208fc87b7d29f6da478c25baac279f140aefe5ea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2p^2q+2pq^2+2q^2r+2qr^2+2r^2p+2rp^2+6pqr = 2(p+q+r)(pq+qr+rp) = 20.\\]\" width=\"569\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting this from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/2/0a2c485ce2dff855b720b70857da36c6ea9a92bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2p^2q+2pq^2+2q^2r+2qr^2+2r^2p+2rp^2+8pqr = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"408\" height=\"18\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecd0c14f94e374fa8efc43edf4e6be1b99985413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2pqr = -16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/b/18bcfd6412e6a13571b0a3749985f0168f5fba0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pqr = -8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" />, which means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are the roots of the cubic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/0/a60a0feb7021ce8e5fc9ddbbfabcf168a10e6fd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 - 5x^2 + 2x + 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" />, and it is not hard to find that these roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The largest of these values is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/3502fb5e69be78d9b9580690026667f60fc47147.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>Extra note: One can also use the identity\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/9/8492e3bcd60334bf026c963b2e6f21114193d37d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(p+q)(q+r)(p+r)=2pqr+\\sum_{sym}p^2q\\]\" width=\"297\" height=\"39\" />\nto compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/7/63795f5ae81b5558afc51ffd1b2e8a7a30d38f30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pqr$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/b/49b30698a4449ad68158b3d77209a74b87a65363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2q+pq^2+q^2r+qr^2+r^2p+rp^2+4pqr = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"355\" height=\"20\" />, use our identity to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/9/499ab01d4d153f55ef55ce91136f7beea798b06a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2pqr+(p+q)(q+r)(p+r)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"255\" height=\"20\" />. Then use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1b687da7c406e8ac50fbb8061425195af418aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q+r=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"17\" /> to rewrite as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/4/5f473b37a3d822eee278f9d089d59e20ebbb2fed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2pqr+(5-p)(5-q)(5-r)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"256\" height=\"20\" />. Expanding and using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/d/3ed7d7274a55143b10aad186ee9bbbbb86eb0ff0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pq+qr+pr=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"17\" /> as well gives the result <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/4/824a77b9a880e9cd54714b89801e7ede58123b03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pqr=-8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>~~ clarkculus\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-values where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/4/864248160d32abf24619d995d2c4892f9832e50c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = x^6 - 10x^5 + 29x^4 - 4x^3 + ax^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"269\" height=\"20\" /> intersects \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/c/dacd48dd2f38d4ec3041c9281285beb6c915937c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = bx + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> are the zeros of\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/f/48fef594db5cee3776c8f1563fcfc82fc2b76144.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x) = x^6 - 10x^5 + 29x^4 - 4x^3 + ax^2 - bx - c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"364\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>We are told the graph lies above the line except at exactly three values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. \nThus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41cfdc781ab823ec638e04df3da3dc2352fcc61f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x) \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and it has exactly three real roots.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> has degree 6 and is always nonnegative, each real root must have even multiplicity. \nBecause there are exactly three real roots and the total multiplicity is 6, each root has multiplicity 2.\n</p><p>So we may write\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/d/86d1fde0ace5ce28ab12a0175374318b09fd0bb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x) = (x-p)^2(x-q)^2(x-r)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"249\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Since the leading coefficient is 1, this equals\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/8/af84898328e5bb5a1a4564e5cac908b89ff05b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^3 + ux^2 + vx + w)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Expanding,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/c/92c5d6cfa3a148396655a3f3ce7c01dd87fa3137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^3 + ux^2 + vx + w)^2 = x^6 + 2u x^5 + (u^2 + 2v)x^4 + (2uv + 2w)x^3 + \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"558\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Matching coefficients with\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bf8b132f7274df32537341ac391ecc5f19263c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^6 - 10x^5 + 29x^4 - 4x^3 + \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"232\" height=\"18\" /> gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/2/cc26ec21815d42987556fb45da0155062d51dc7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2u = -10 \\Rightarrow u = -5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"164\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/c/67c4c1d7c1540d61fc0c847bbdf0c85e5b1f7f7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u^2 + 2v = 29 \\Rightarrow 25 + 2v = 29 \\Rightarrow v = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"304\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/7/687fdaad241a89a416c5ba8ab4970a7718f5d780.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2uv + 2w = -4 \\Rightarrow 2(-5)(2) + 2w = -4 \\Rightarrow -20 + 2w = -4 \\Rightarrow 2w = 16 \\Rightarrow w = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"635\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Thus,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/1702fc739a062ae78f2807a24af329a8c7a70e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x) = (x^3 - 5x^2 + 2x + 8)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"222\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Now factor the cubic. Testing rational roots, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e7d65cfa316d639c9267398009812f3eb45fea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> works:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/7/847c91daf851701a02fdb09cb90517ff450d390a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^3 - 5(4^2) + 2(4) + 8 = 64 - 80 + 8 + 8 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"345\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Dividing gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c11ce0fab5b962bbea03456aa2681e5e246d53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 - 5x^2 + 2x + 8 = (x-4)(x^2 - x - 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"318\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Factor the quadratic:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/2/622aeff4447570e62d9631249e4161abbe88525d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - x - 2 = (x-2)(x+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"220\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>So\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/1/d11fb242fb857f64910561bf75040813025b49f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x) = (x-4)^2 (x-2)^2 (x+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"250\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>The intersection points are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/5/3e52374f15dc306de746d5c48b0e2e9aa1dc1254.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -1, 2, 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>The largest is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c4c6c07150a0f6e56b0a6e198d1d19155dfe96c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"22\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~~bilbaogobao\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/8/168e74f4d54ead2f6ac321d8255629749ce86fed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x^6-10x^5+29x^4-4x^3+ax^2-bx-c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"373\" height=\"20\" /> has exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> roots. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/1/8d1306722e26a2af24a6cd13e0f0101b72120efd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = (kx^3+lx^2+mx+n)^2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"246\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/3/dd3f7a63f57ea6be9b78c7fcd3aeab4a691ae455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2x^6+2klx^5+(2km+l^2)x^4+2(kn+lm)x^3+ax^2-bx-c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"509\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>By matching the coefficients of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> terms, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/f/4df8815ffd2def4759a7809cde63bbaf1f40d349.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2 = 1, 2kl = -10, 2km+l^2 = 29, 2kn+2lm = -4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"402\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Solving the equations above, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sets of solutions; first set of which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/d/d0dc81754ce4db23546a7f200153337283211fe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1, l = -5, m = 2, n = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"216\" height=\"18\" />. Second set of which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa68eb201a047f02c59f535f3d5a95783cfc4ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = -1, l = 5, m = -2, n = -8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"245\" height=\"18\" />. After squaring both sets, they are the same i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2f04de590563e069949a4738179dc07b129d7c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3-5x^2+2x+8 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>This is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc00cdf36b2f56346ddeaf001f13c22595589975.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-4)(x-2)(x+1) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"203\" height=\"20\" />. The largest root is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c5398ac29083f4905f847444f89a4e8d0c015b1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{(A) 4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~Arcticturn\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> values in the coordinates of which these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> polynomials intersect is the same as the zeroes of<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/4/b449dcda2e1562a62d515f869a8a873594ad0d38.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(x)=x^6-10x^5+29x^4-4x^3+ax^2-bx-c.\\]\" width=\"370\" height=\"20\" />Since there are only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> intersections, they must all be double roots. So, we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/8/e385783d8054cca0db45c6c43b95241ff38255b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r,s,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> be the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />. We let,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/3/443f794d15fe628ba6c463c9b624c62a803060e7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-r)(x-s)(x-t)=x^3-ux^2+vx-w\\]\" width=\"332\" height=\"20\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/4/0143d1b2c5ff815c1895f14e7b1768dbf6c7d107.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Longrightarrow [(x-r)(x-s)(x-t)]^2=x^6-10x^5+29x^4-4x^3+ax^2-bx-c\\]\" width=\"539\" height=\"20\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/a/11a7baec09f970ae90ea221f27449412d2363869.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Longrightarrow \\sqrt{x^6-10x^5+29x^4-4x^3+ax^2-bx-c} = x^3-ux^2+vx-w\\]\" width=\"522\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/0/9c0ef88d0368cd308774d885bbbc2ec3c910e3bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Longrightarrow x^6-10x^5+29x^4-4x^3+ax^2-bx-c=(x^3-ux^2+vx-w)^2\\]\" width=\"527\" height=\"20\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/e/61efbd1076bd219fffc48dd53c79872a8659824d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Longrightarrow x^6-10x^5+29x^4-4x^3+ax^2-bx-c=x^6-(2u)x^5+(u^2+2v)x^4-(2w+2uv)x^3+...\\]\" width=\"632\" height=\"20\" />We don't really care about the other coefficients because they aren't known. So, comparing coefficients, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/f/d7ff545b42de12a7d9576b5873e1158e8edab708.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u,v,w)=(5,2,-8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" />. So, we have<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/7/58733ec83864ae1e758dad21f80fc5cbfea7d881.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-r)(x-s)(x-t)=x^3-5x^2+2x+8.\\]\" width=\"330\" height=\"20\" />Now, we can use RRT to finish from here. Factoring the polynomial gives<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/b/8ab43bda01ba6e7be888950ecd5f85d564d29f59.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^3-5x^2+2x+8=(x+1)(x-2)(x-4),\\]\" width=\"335\" height=\"20\" />so, our largets root is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e93ecd8ba0c38820f6115d310bebd0377c00e01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 4}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"62\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>-jb2015007\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A\" title=\"2010 AMC 12A\">2010 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2010 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;